Statistically speaking, the amount of books in this library, as much as any well established library, is so numerous that no person would be able to sit down and read all of them in a single lifetime.
Perhaps a smaller library could be digested with proper dedication, but you know what "they" say\:\
"No one reads books anymore."\
Even if such a library were conquered, what use would there be for harboring such vast amounts of "knowledge?"
But, I digress. Even though it was much the duty of machines to keep track of vast quantities of data, you have no access, no permissions to this knowledge anyway.
